<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Katō Yoshiaki</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1563–1631</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as Kato Yoshiaki</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Katō Yoshiaki was a Japanese <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/daimyo">daimyo</a> and naval commander. One of the 'Seven Spears of Shizugatake' who served <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/toyotomi-hideyoshi">Toyotomi Hideyoshi</a>, he commanded fleets in the invasions of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/korea">Korea</a> and built Matsuyama Castle on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shikoku">Shikoku</a>. He sided with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tokugawa-ieyasu">Tokugawa Ieyasu</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-sekigahara">Sekigahara</a> in 1600, and in 1627 he was transferred to the domain of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aizu">Aizu</a> with 400,000 koku.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kato-yoshiaki.jpg" alt="Katō Yoshiaki" width="320" height="270" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kat%C5%8D_Yoshiaki.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
